This repository holds two different kinds of work, and they carry two different
licences. Nothing here is unlicensed.

## Software — Apache License 2.0

Full text: [`LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)

Applies to:

- every `.py` file, and the code cells of the notebooks;
- the z3st case definitions (`.yaml`, `.geo`) and their run scripts, where they are
  distributed.

Same licence as [z3st](https://github.com/giozu/z3st), which this material runs on,
so the two repositories can be read and reused under one rule.

## Teaching material — CC BY-NC 4.0

Notice and links: [`LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt)

Applies to everything else: the notebooks and all the prose, the `README.md` files
included.

Credit the author, link back, say what you changed, and do not sell it. Teaching a
course from it is the intended use.

## The one place the split is awkward

A notebook is teaching material that contains code. To remove any doubt: **the code
cells inside the notebooks may also be used under Apache-2.0**, on the same terms as
the `.py` files. Take a function you need without wondering which licence follows it.

## Not in this repository

Reference solutions and anything related to grading are not published here, under
any licence.
